  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC Goma Acute Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">January 2025 has witnessed an increased violence and conflict in Goma, DR Congo and its surroundings. This current escalation comes at the back of fighting that broke out in eastern DRC. On 27 Jan. most of Goma town was captured by M23. This has led to displacement of more than 400,000 people. Basic services such as water and electricity were largely paralyzed and existing shelter camps were dismantled. Vulnerable women, children, of which unaccompanied minors and elderly are now living in overcrowded and precarious conditions with limited access to food, water, and essential services.</narrative>
  </description>
